<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n8463" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνεπί-φθονος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>without reproach,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔγχος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Tr.</u>
					1033
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. ἐστι πᾶσιν</span> it
			is <i>no reproach to</i> any one, <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				6.83
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>R.</u>
				612b
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Epicur.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				161
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὕτω γάρ μοι . . ἀνεπιφθονώτατον
					εἰπεῖν</span>”
				<i>least invidious,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.
					18.321
				</span></i>
			; <i>ungrudging,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔπαινος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Onos.
					<u>Praef.</u>
					10
				</span></i>
			. Adv. [
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὴν ἀρχὴν] ἀνεπιφθόνως κατεστήσατο</span>”
				<i>so as not to create odium,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					Th.
					6.54
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Cam.</u>
				1
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. εἰπεῖν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Isoc.
					15.8
				</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
